    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18142" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφ-άπτω</span></b> , aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφῆψα,</span> imper. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄφαψον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					<u>Bel.</u>
					65.37
				</span></i>
			:—<i>fasten from</i> or <i>upon,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅμματα ἀπάψας</span>
			<i>having tied</i> knots <i>on a string,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.98
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Fist.</u>
				4
			</span></i>:— 
				Med.
			, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Pr.</u>
				3.3
			</span></i>, al.:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be hung on, hang on,</i>
			pf.
			part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαμμένος</span> (
				Ion.
			 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφημμ-</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.121
			</span></i>.
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ́; ἀφημμένος ἐκ ποδεώνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					22.52
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph. of
			argument, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				16.82
			</span></i>.</div>
